# Galera rejoin timeline — LIVE captures, MariaDB 11.8.8 + galera 26.4.27,
# 3-node local cluster (galera1/2/3, ports 3341/3342/3343), 2026-10-02.
# One line per poll round: nN=<wsrep_local_state_comment>,q:<recv_queue>,lc:<last_committed>,dc:<desync_count>.
#
# EXPERIMENT 1 — SST (forced): galera3 stopped at seqno 70, ~128 MB written on
# galera1 (gcache.size=64M overrun: cached_downto moved to 142 > 70), galera3
# restarted. n3 was connection-refused 11:58:37→11:58:54 (the whole observed
# window); the rsync SST daemon was observed at 11:58:53.
#
# TRUTH vs the old assumption: the joiner's mariadbd REFUSED TCP CONNECTIONS
# (ERROR 2002) for the entire transfer — no 1047, no Joining/Joined state was
# ever visible over SQL; the only SQL-visible signal was the DONOR
# (galera1 = Donor/Desynced with desync=OFF, desync_count=1, captured in
# tests/fixtures/galera-status-mariadb118-donor.txt).
